# Build-context hygiene for the `COPY . .` in Dockerfile.
#
# Without this the daemon receives ~865MB (.dart_tool alone is ~521MB, build/
# ~335MB), and worse, the HOST's build/ and .dart_tool/ land in /app: those
# carry macOS absolute paths in package_config.json, and stale web artifacts
# from an older build config can survive `flutter build web` and be copied to
# nginx. Everything excluded here is either regenerated inside the image by
# `flutter pub get` / `flutter build web`, or has no business in a build.

.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore

# Host build output and tool state - regenerated in the image.
build/
.dart_tool/
.hermes/

# This app takes its config from --dart-define, never from a .env file, so
# none of these are build inputs. Without them a developer who keeps a local
# .env or .env.local copies real credentials into the builder layer. The glob
# is deliberate: .gitignore keeps `.env.example` tracked as documentation, but
# the image has no use for it either.
.env*

# Editor and IDE state.
.idea/
*.iml

# Docs and CI descriptors are not build inputs.
README.md
LICENSE
